{
  "name": "Turn an RSS feed into scheduled social posts with Nadia",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Turn an RSS feed into scheduled social posts\n\nEvery hour this workflow reads an RSS feed, keeps only the items published since the last run, asks an AI model for a caption written for social, and schedules the post on a Nadia channel in the next free slot of your posting schedule.\n\nNothing is published immediately: each item lands in the calendar at a slot Nadia picks, so a burst of ten articles does not become ten posts in ten minutes.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. **Schedule Trigger** fires every hour.\n2. **RSS Read** fetches the feed.\n3. **Filter** drops anything older than the interval, so an item is never posted twice.\n4. **Basic LLM Chain** rewrites the title and summary as a caption.\n5. **Nadia** creates the post with *Use Next Free Slot* on, which asks the API for the next open slot of that channel.\n\n### Setup\n\n1. Add your **Nadia** credential: API key from Settings -> Developers, host `https://app.usenadia.com/api`.\n2. Open the **Nadia** node and pick your channel from the dropdown, then fill the channel settings it loads.\n3. Set the feed URL in **RSS Read**.\n4. Add credentials for the model you want in **Basic LLM Chain**.\n\n### Customize\n\nSwap the Filter for a keyword check to post only some items, or set the node to *Draft* to review everything in the calendar before it goes out.",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 620
      },
      "id": "sticky-note",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Read the feed\nHourly, keep only what is new since the last run.",
        "width": 420,
        "height": 240,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "sticky-note1",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Write the caption\nThe article title and summary become a caption written for social.",
        "width": 300,
        "height": 240,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "sticky-note2",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        420,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Schedule it\nNadia picks the next free slot of that channel.",
        "width": 300,
        "height": 240,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "sticky-note3",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        760,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hoursInterval": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "every-hour",
      "name": "Every hour",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://example.com/feed.xml",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "rss-read",
      "name": "RSS Read",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.rssFeedRead",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.isoDate }}",
              "rightValue": "={{ $now.minus(1, 'hour').toISO() }}",
              "operator": {
                "type": "dateTime",
                "operation": "after"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "only-new-items",
      "name": "Only new items",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.filter",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        460,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Write a social media caption for this article. Two or three sentences, no hashtags, no emoji, end with the link.\n\nTitle: {{ $json.title }}\nSummary: {{ $json.contentSnippet }}\nLink: {{ $json.link }}",
        "messages": {}
      },
      "id": "write-the-caption",
      "name": "Write the caption",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.4,
      "position": [
        700,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "createPost",
        "channelId": "",
        "type": "schedule",
        "useFreeSlot": true,
        "content": "={{ $json.text }}",
        "media": "",
        "settings": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "value": {}
        },
        "additionalFields": {
          "shortLink": true
        }
      },
      "id": "nadia",
      "name": "Nadia",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-nadia.nadia",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        960,
        0
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "nadiaApi": {
          "id": "REPLACE",
          "name": "Nadia account"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Every hour": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "RSS Read",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "RSS Read": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Only new items",
